{
  "dom_id": "step-e10876",
  "name": "Example: Evaluating an Accumulation Function",
  "problem": "Calculate $F(\\pi)$ where $\\displaystyle F(x) = \\int_1^x \\dfrac 1 t\\,\\textrm d t.$",
  "worked_solution": "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=\\pi,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\!\\left(\\pi\\right) = \\int_{1}^{\\pi} \\dfrac{1}{t} \\, \\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\pi ) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|\\,{|}_{1}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\pi -\\operatorname{ln}\u20611 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
